¶ great peculiarity of Mr. Poole's board, ¶ ]\Ir. Brown differs from it entirely, is in ¶ introduction of the columns "5 and "6, ¶ containing natural Sevenths, and their ¶ as it were, with the col. 7 ¶ ]\Ir. Brown alone uses) in three short ¶ digitals, placed beside the black, and hence ¶ the same length. They are placed from ¶ to back, as red, yellow, blue — that is, as ¶ Sevenths and a Third, which belong to ¶ different keys. Thus in fig. 68, to the ¶ of the black digital for E-^ (marked e), lie ¶ coloured digitals, 1) the red^^t* (of which ¶ name is not marked in the fig.), the natural ¶ of the tonic in the key of 7^; 2) the ¶ "D^ (marked d"), the natural Seventh of

